<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Lamberson Butte</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:198-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.321340" lon="-121.617170"><ele>1299.1</ele><name>Clark Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:clark-creek-sno-park (on OR 35; lot unmapped); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 197; quote: From Clark Creek Sno-Park ski a trail 150 yards to the junction where the Clark Creek Trail starts. Here turn left</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.324222" lon="-121.620670"><ele>1325.7</ele><name>Old Elk Meadows Trail, east end</name><desc>source: OSM way 146985885 'Old Elk Meadows Trail' east end (the 1.2-mile built-for-skiing trail); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 197; quote: at first along a 1.2-mile built-for-skiing trail to the Clark Creek single-log bridge</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.328930" lon="-121.630932"><ele>1387.7</ele><name>Joins the summer Elk Meadows Trail (Clark Creek bridge)</name><desc>source: OSM: Old Elk Meadows Trail meets Elk Meadows Trail #645; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 197; quote: to the Clark Creek single-log bridge where it joins the summer Elk Meadows hiking trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.334935" lon="-121.626145"><ele>1405.3</ele><name>Newton Creek crossing</name><desc>source: OSM node 1601784626, end of Newton Creek Trail #646 on #645; DEM 4,610 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 199; book_elev_ft: 4640; quote: ski to Newton Creek via the Elk Meadows Trail. Cross the creek</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.340871" lon="-121.623195"><ele>1607.3</ele><name>Elk Mountain Saddle</name><desc>source: OSM junction Elk Meadows Trail #645 x Gnarl Ridge Trail #652; DEM 5,273 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 199; book_elev_ft: 5260; quote: follow the unmarked summer hiking trail upward steeply as it zigzags to Elk Mountain Saddle at 5,260 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.351727" lon="-121.633211"><ele>1724.0</ele><name>Gnarl Ridge Trail meets the Timberline Trail</name><desc>source: OSM junction Gnarl Ridge Trail #652 x Timberline Trail #600; DEM 5,656 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 200; quote: From the saddle follow as well as possible the obscure summer hiking trail through open, then thick, stands of trees</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.358383" lon="-121.639982"><ele>1891.2</ele><name>Leave the Timberline Trail east of the butte</name><desc>source: OSM node 3808835604 on Timberline Trail #600, where it turns north-west round the butte, 550 m E of the summit; DEM 6,205 ft; DEM rises steadily west along the ridge crest to the summit (6,280 / 6,385 / 6,495 / 6,625); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 200; quote: From the saddle it is 3 miles to the top of the butte ... map 42 draws the dotted route straight up the ridge to the butte</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.359037" lon="-121.646923"><ele>2019.3</ele><name>Lamberson Butte</name><desc>source: OSM peak node 357311568; DEM 6,625 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 200; book_elev_ft: 6633; quote: At 6,633 feet, the butte is 1,370 feet above the saddle and 2,400 feet above the sno-park</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Lamberson Butte</name><desc>1. Clark Creek Sno-Park -&gt; Old Elk Meadows Trail, east end: straight (low), 0.26 mi | 2. Old Elk Meadows Trail, east end -&gt; Joins the summer Elk Meadows Trail (Clark Creek bridge): osm (medium), 0.65 mi | 3. Joins the summer Elk Meadows Trail (Clark Creek bridge) -&gt; Newton Creek crossing: osm (high), 0.52 mi | 4. Newton Creek crossing -&gt; Elk Mountain Saddle: osm (high), 0.97 mi | 5. Elk Mountain Saddle -&gt; Gnarl Ridge Trail meets the Timberline Trail: osm (medium), 1.00 mi | 6. Gnarl Ridge Trail meets the Timberline Trail -&gt; Leave the Timberline Trail east of the butte: osm (medium), 0.87 mi | 7. Leave the Timberline Trail east of the butte -&gt; Lamberson Butte: straight (medium), 0.34 mi</desc>
